  "findings": "Directly inspected all 16 with/without navigation screenshots at 320px and 390px. With the current candidate applied, the mobile top-bar submenus are contained inside the viewport at both widths and every item is legible; no horizontal overflow or clipping. The masthead renders the theme genuine scanline wordmark logo (the --img-logo data-URI asset embedded in the candidate CSS); it is byte-identical in appearance to the certified 2026-10-02 trusted navigation capture of this theme, so the striped rendering is the theme design, not a defect. The without variant is the unchanged native Wikidot rendering of the same frozen target snapshot. This capture replaces the compact fixture navigation evidence, which still bound the pre-fix candidate CSS digest."
